// #465: an unknown method on an INT receiver was reported and then silently
// DELETED, and the build exited 0 with a wrong answer.
//
// Measured on dev @ 3dd65450:
//     x = 42 ; x.nope_zzz()
//     wyn check  ->  "no errors"                                   exit 0
//     wyn build  ->  "Error: Unknown method ..." then "✓ Built"    exit 0
//     ./a.out    ->  ran with the call removed                     exit 0
// The same program with a STRING or ARRAY receiver exited 1, because those two
// receivers are rejected at check time (#426) while int/float/bool are not: the
// checker keeps them lenient on purpose (TYPE_INT is its fallback type for
// anything it could not resolve), so the question is only answerable in codegen -
// and codegen had no way to fail the build. See src/codegen.c's codegen_error.
//
// THE ASSERTION IS THE EXIT CODE, and it has to be. The diagnostic text was
// already printed before the fix, so an error-text-only gate (EXPECT_ERR alone)
// would have passed on the broken compiler. EXPECT_FAIL is the arm that was red.
//
// Accept arm (a rule that rejects everything would also satisfy this file):
// tests/regression/unknown_method_scalar_accepted.wyn.
// Sibling receivers: unknown_method_on_float_rejected.wyn,
// unknown_method_on_bool_rejected.wyn.
// EXPECT_FAIL:
// EXPECT_ERR: for type 'int'
x = 42
x.nope_zzz()
print(x)
